  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Calm and dry weather conditions return\nover Nevada today through Sunday as the first weather system moves\neastward over Utah. Temperatures today will be several degrees\nbelow normal with highs in the 40s to low 50s. Tomorrow,\ntemperatures warm up to near normal temperatures in the 50s. Winds\nwill be generally light with a few breezy gusts up to 20-25 mph in\ncentral Nevada.\n\nMonday, the momentary break from the weather is expected to end as\na second weather system pushes into Nevada from the northwest.\nIncreasing chances for additional precipitation and high elevated\nsnow with snowfall expected to reach higher passes and summits as\nsnow levels start around 7000 feet and drop to 6500 feet\novernight. Northern Nevada summits have a 20-30% probability of \nseeing one inch of snowfall while central Nevada summits are \nseeing a 50-85% chance of one inch of snowfall (highest \nprobabilities along the US-50 corridor). Much of the precipitation\nand snow is expected to be on Monday, with some lingering showers\nlasting into Tuesday. This weather system is also expected to \nbring in much colder temperatures behind the storm front with \nhighs on Monday being a few degrees below normal in the upper 40s,\nwith Tuesday expected to see temperatures up to 10 degrees below \nnormal in places as highs will only be in the 30s to low 40s.\n\nTuesday afternoon, calmer weather conditions return, however the\ncalm is not expected to last long as a third weather system is\nexpected to impact Nevada Wednesday morning with additional chances\nfor precipitation and snow that will last through Thursday.\nTemperatures expected to continue to fall as colder air continues\nto move into Nevada, with highs staying up to 10 degrees below\nnormal in the 30s to low 40s Wednesday, with Thursday expected to\nbe up to 10-15 degrees below normal with highs in the 30s.\n\nFriday, the system will weaken and move eastward, allowing a short\nwave ridge to move back in over Nevada, bringing back calmer\nweather conditions. High temperatures will still remain up to\n10-15 degrees below normal staying in the 30s. As of right now,\nthe calm weather conditions are expected to go into the weekend,\nhowever models are showing another low pressure system to the\nnorthwest along the Pacific coastline. Current model runs are\nkeeping the system to the northwest through the weekend which will\nbring in a southwesterly flow over Nevada, but no signs of\nprecipitation as of right now.",
